# Runtime environment for the hosted instance. Copy to gev.env (git-ignored by
# deploy/.gitignore) and uncomment what you use. Names only; no real values here.
#
# This is the hosting subset. The root .env.example is the full reference for
# every variable (rate limits, CCTV packs, model ids, tuning).
#
# Everything is optional: with nothing set the app runs on keyless sources.
# Leave unused lines commented out rather than blank.

# --- Access -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Hostname(s) the instance is served on, comma-separated. Required when it is
# reached by name (a tunnel or reverse proxy); IP addresses and localhost are
# always accepted. Wildcards are ignored.
# GEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=globe.example.com

# --- Server-side keys that work behind a tunnel or reverse proxy -------------
# Live ships (free: aisstream.io)
# AISSTREAM_API_KEY=
# Live active fires (free: firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key)
# FIRMS_MAP_KEY=
# More flight-polling credits (free: opensky-network.org); anonymous without
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Server-side keys upstream serves to direct connections only -------------
# Requests that arrive with reverse-proxy headers (X-Forwarded-For, CF-Ray, ...)
# are answered 403 on these routes on purpose (SECURITY.md). They work over an
# SSH port-forward or a direct private-network address, not through a tunnel.
# Voice, typed chat and the HUD summary (metered: platform.openai.com). Set a
# monthly usage limit at OpenAI first.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Google place search and geocoding. IP-restrict this key to the host and scope
# it to Places + Geocoding + Street View Static (metered).
# GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_API_KEY=
# Live traffic flow (free tier: my.tomtom.com/keys)
# TOMTOM_API_KEY=
# News layer, Local section (free plan: worldnewsapi.com/console; read its
# caching terms in the root .env.example first)
# WORLDNEWSAPI_KEY=

# --- Browser keys are NOT set here -------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY, CESIUM_ION_TOKEN and MAPILLARY_CLIENT_TOKEN are compiled
# into the bundle when the image is built (repository secrets of the same names
# for the workflow, or --secret on a manual docker build). Setting them here
# does not change what the browser gets.

# --- Throttles (per client address, in-memory; not billing caps) -------------
# Behind a tunnel every visitor shares one address, so these act as a whole-
# instance cap. Defaults: 30 and 120 requests a minute.
# GEV_RATELIMIT_OPENAI_PER_MIN=30
# GEV_RATELIMIT_GOOGLE_PER_MIN=60
